<title>USA: Greyhound ups credit facility to $105 mln.</title>
<headline>Greyhound ups credit facility to $105 mln.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greyhound Lines Inc said on Tuesday that its lending group, led by Foothill Capital Corp, a subsidiary of Norwest Corp, agreed to increase its revolving credit to $105 million from $80 million, and extend the maturity of the facility to June 30, 1999.</p>
<p>The expanded facility is expected to close by early December, it said.</p>
<p>Greyhound also said that the First National BankBoston joined the credit facility.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
